  <title>Cumulative exposure of Southern Right Whales to key threats (NESP MaC 3.15)</title>
  <description>Generated from GeoTIFF</description>
  <abstract>Spatial threat layers representing ship strike, chronic underwater noise, pollution, entanglement and climate change were standardised to a 10 × 10 km grid. Exposure of Southern right whales to each of these threats was calculated by combining the occurrence of tagged whales within each grid cell with the corresponding threat intensity.&#xd;
&#xd;
This layer package contains the exposure to each of the five component threats, and cumulative threat-exposure, each normalised from 0 (no exposure) to 1 (maximum exposure). Select from the available styles to navigate between exposure to each component threat.</abstract>
